WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:06.867
Hello, and welcome back. So far,
we've explored the National Data tab,

2
00:00:06.867 --> 00:00:10.512
including topics from
community living to economics.

3
00:00:10.512 --> 00:00:15.840
In this session, we're going to zoom in
and take a deeper dive on city data.

4
00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:18.415
Right now, we're on the home page,

5
00:00:18.415 --> 00:00:22.670
so let's start by clicking on City
Data on the top center banner.

6
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:31.089
Previously, we explored national data. This
was information collected by each state.

7
00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:37.799
Whereas city data is specific to each city
in each state. It's much more specific.

8
00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:43.120
Before we dive into the data, I want to
orient you to the setup of the page.

9
00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:45.420
Each page will have a map.

10
00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:50.787
General information on the number
of residents in the city and the

11
00:00:50.787 --> 00:00:54.479
number of residents and percentages
of people with disabilities.

12
00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.379
And then below, there's a summary
table that provides information on

13
00:00:59.379 --> 00:01:04.209
disability demographics and ADA-PARC
key indicators that we've seen before.

14
00:01:04.319 --> 00:01:08.929
Including community participation, work
and economics, and community living.

15
00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:13.600
Let's start by looking in the map.

16
00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:17.329
In the corner, it says Chicago, Illinois.

17
00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:23.270
We have a key in the top right corner that
tells us exactly what these colors means.

18
00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:27.222
In this case, it's the percent
of people with disabilities.

19
00:01:27.222 --> 00:01:30.345
The map shows us the city
we selected, Chicago,

20
00:01:30.345 --> 00:01:35.596
broken down into different areas called
census tracts. These areas are colored,

21
00:01:35.596 --> 00:01:38.920
with darker colored areas
showing places that have

22
00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:42.110
a higher percentage of
people with disabilities.

23
00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:46.240
And lighter colors show a lower
percentage of people with disabilities.

24
00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:48.899
This gray represents not applicable.

25
00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:51.627
This either means that there's no people

26
00:01:51.627 --> 00:01:54.451
with disabilities who
live in that district,

27
00:01:54.451 --> 00:01:57.789
or it means that there wasn't
enough data collected.

28
00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:00.990
This can be one of the
downfalls of city data.

29
00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:03.539
There might not be enough data collected.

30
00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:07.209
On the left side of the map,
there's a plus and a minus sign.

31
00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:09.765
The minus sign zooms out the map,

32
00:02:09.765 --> 00:02:13.459
so you can see more of the
area, but less specifics.

33
00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.032
The plus sign zooms in the map,

34
00:02:16.032 --> 00:02:20.280
so you can see more specifics,
but less of the entire city.

35
00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:25.009
You can see that in the west of the city.

36
00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:28.729
In the south sides, it's
represented by these darker colors.

37
00:02:28.729 --> 00:02:32.531
So there's more people with
disabilities who live in these areas.

38
00:02:32.531 --> 00:02:36.859
Whereas, when you drag your mouse and
go up north, there's lighter colors.

39
00:02:36.859 --> 00:02:41.480
There's… meaning there's less people with
disabilities who live in these areas.

40
00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:45.613
You might start to wonder and reflect
on your own cities and think,

41
00:02:45.613 --> 00:02:48.236
why are there higher or
lower percentages of

42
00:02:48.236 --> 00:02:50.739
people with disabilities in certain areas?

43
00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:55.015
To find more specific information
about disability data,

44
00:02:55.015 --> 00:02:57.340
we will scroll down to the summary table.

45
00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:02.611
This is a little different than what we've
seen before, but it's the same concept.

46
00:03:02.611 --> 00:03:07.037
It tells us information about disability
demographics, disability types,

47
00:03:07.037 --> 00:03:09.004
and the ADA-PARC key indicators,

48
00:03:09.004 --> 00:03:12.570
which are topics we've discussed
in the National Data tab.

49
00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:17.780
I will briefly review each category to
help us understand how to read the data.

50
00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:21.179
Let's start under Who
Reports a Disability.

51
00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:25.979
Let's start with the race
and ethnicity category.

52
00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:31.335
Each box provides the percent of people
with disabilities in that specific race,

53
00:03:31.335 --> 00:03:36.119
as well as the number of people with
disabilities who identify as that race.

54
00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:41.285
For example, 5.1% of Black people
have a disability in Chicago,

55
00:03:41.285 --> 00:03:45.558
which is about 137,000 Black
people with disabilities.

56
00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:50.860
This is a much higher number compared
to any other race in Chicago.

57
00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:54.165
Let's move on to the next category.

58
00:03:54.165 --> 00:03:58.369
The U.S. Census tracks data based
on the terms male and female.

59
00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:02.602
Even though they may be outdated,
these are the terms we will use,

60
00:04:02.602 --> 00:04:05.619
because this is what the
data's been collected on.

61
00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:11.734
Next, you can find the percentage of people
with disabilities in each age group.

62
00:04:11.734 --> 00:04:14.359
I will let you explore
this section on your own.

63
00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:18.720
Lastly, let's scroll down and
explore disability types.

64
00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:23.269
There are different disability types
that are tracked by the census.

65
00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:29.030
There's hearing, vision, cognitive,
ambulatory, self-care, and independent living.

66
00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:31.733
These are all topics
we've explored before,

67
00:04:31.733 --> 00:04:34.736
so let's choose self-care
disability in this case.

68
00:04:34.736 --> 00:04:39.240
A self-care disability is when a person
has difficulty bathing or dressing.

69
00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:44.388
About 61,000 people in Chicago
have a self-care disability.

70
00:04:44.388 --> 00:04:47.599
So that's about 2.4% of the population.

71
00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:51.950
Now, let's compare this to
independent living disabilities.

72
00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:55.168
There are about 123,000
people with disability…

73
00:04:55.168 --> 00:04:58.455
with independent living
disabilities in Chicago.

74
00:04:58.455 --> 00:05:00.920
That's about 4.6% of the population.

75
00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:04.549
That's a higher percentage
than self-care in Chicago.

76
00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:08.320
Next, let's explore
community participation.

77
00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:12.173
The first category is insurance.

78
00:05:12.173 --> 00:05:16.324
You can find data on how many
people in each city have insurance,

79
00:05:16.324 --> 00:05:20.539
have private or public insurance,
or do not have insurance at all.

80
00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.814
This data is divided
by age groups as well,

81
00:05:23.814 --> 00:05:26.680
so you can find very specific information.

82
00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:29.755
You can also find
information on education,

83
00:05:29.755 --> 00:05:34.583
specifically how many people with
disabilities have a high school diploma,

84
00:05:34.583 --> 00:05:35.888
a bachelor's degree,

85
00:05:35.888 --> 00:05:40.129
as well as the number of people
who did not graduate high school.

86
00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:43.932
Lastly, you can find data on
the types of transportation

87
00:05:43.932 --> 00:05:46.330
people with disabilities
use to get to work.

88
00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:50.749
Next, we're going to explore
the work and economic category.

89
00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:57.072
In this section, you can find
information about employment.

90
00:05:57.072 --> 00:06:01.577
So, you can find information about the
number of people who are employed,

91
00:06:01.577 --> 00:06:03.429
either part-time or full-time.

92
00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:08.320
Unemployed, looking for work,
or out of the labor force.

93
00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:13.840
You can find information on the median
earnings of residents over the age of 16,

94
00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:17.468
You can find information on
the number and percentage

95
00:06:17.468 --> 00:06:20.475
of people who live below
the federal poverty line,

96
00:06:20.475 --> 00:06:22.520
broken up by different age groups.

97
00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:26.205
As well as information on
housing cost burdens for

98
00:06:26.205 --> 00:06:29.329
people who are renters
or who have a mortgage.

99
00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:34.150
Lastly, you can find information
in community living.

100
00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:38.412
This will show you information on
the percentage of people who have a

101
00:06:38.412 --> 00:06:42.366
housing choice voucher and whose
head of household has a disability,

102
00:06:42.366 --> 00:06:44.925
as well as people who
live in public housing

103
00:06:44.925 --> 00:06:47.309
whose head of household has a disability.

104
00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:51.345
Lastly, I want to show you how
to change the city and the state

105
00:06:51.345 --> 00:06:54.579
so that you can find information
that's important to you.

106
00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:57.575
You'll scroll back to the
top, and under state,

107
00:06:57.575 --> 00:07:00.630
you're gonna click on your
state or your territory.

108
00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:03.800
In this example, I'll
click on Puerto Rico.

109
00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:06.300
To the right of this is the city,

110
00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:09.320
so you'll click on the city
that you want to explore.

111
00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:12.340
In this case, I'll focus on San Juan.

112
00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:16.756
You know that a new map has
been generated when you can see

113
00:07:16.756 --> 00:07:20.249
that name reflected on the top
left corner of the screen.

114
00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:22.892
To download any of this information,

115
00:07:22.892 --> 00:07:26.710
you can click on the download button
on the top right corner of the screen.

116
00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:30.827
In this video, we explored
information on city data,

117
00:07:30.827 --> 00:07:35.879
the key indicators, and how to explore
the map. Thanks for tuning in!
